<h1>Privacy</h1>
<p class="last-checked">Last updated November 18, 2026</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is static files served by <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/about-github-pages" rel="nofollow noopener">GitHub Pages</a>. GitHub receives the normal request data any web server gets, such as your IP address.</li>
<li><strong>Analytics.</strong> The site uses <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/about/" rel="nofollow noopener">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>, which is cookieless and doesn't track individuals. Cloudflare says it does not collect or use your visitors' personal data. We see totals such as page views and page load times, not who you are.</li>
<li><strong>Search.</strong> The search box uses Pagefind, which runs in your browser against files on this site. What you type is not sent to us.</li>
<li><strong>Cookies and personal information.</strong> The site itself sets no cookies and collects no personal information. There are no forms and no accounts, and the site does not ask for your details.</li>
<li><strong>Links out.</strong> Links go to NHTSA and other sites with their own privacy policies. If you click an outbound retailer or affiliate link, that company or its affiliate network may set its own cookies to credit the referral, under its own privacy policy. Affiliate links are off today (see the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> and <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a>).</li>
<li><strong>Contact.</strong> <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact }}">{{ site.contact }}</a></li>
</ul>
